      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-22"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-6",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "You can open it yourself — the publish ref is a git branch",
      "prov:value": "WHAT IT COST: twelve navbar tiles shipped pointing at the ORIGIN rather than\nthe site, because their href carried no `baseurl` (#801).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#801"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-7",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "You can open it yourself — the publish ref is a git branch",
      "prov:value": "Over a hundred green\ngates were fine with it, and the owner found it by clicking one — which is\nexactly `rptk`'s shape one layer out."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-8",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "You can open it yourself — the publish ref is a git branch",
      "prov:value": "**A preview that shares with the live site falls back to it.** Since\n2026-10-31 (owner: *\"if asset not changed in staging then link to main\nasset\"*; `cat-harness-tools/scripts/staging-share.ts`) a preview stores only\nthe files that differ from the live site, and its `staging-sw.js` serves the\nrest from the live root in the browser.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-9",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "You can open it yourself — the publish ref is a git branch",
      "prov:value": "That is precisely how #801's e2e\nstayed green over the defect.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#801"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-10",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Report the absent count, and read it before anything else",
      "prov:value": "This page's own technique produced, on a deploy that was in fact correct:"
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-11",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Report the absent count, and read it before anything else",
      "prov:value": "`dh4f` is this repository's name for scanning nothing and reporting it clean."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-12",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "The commit in the bot's comment is NOT your branch head",
      "prov:value": "Measured 2026-09-21, by getting it wrong in this skill's own first use.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-21"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-13",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Finding your way on the review page (bean `eb4l`)",
      "prov:value": "- By the owner's ruling it is **on the review page only**."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-14",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Finding your way on the review page (bean `eb4l`)",
      "prov:value": "The \"no toc\"\n    ruling for normal pages stands."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-15",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Finding your way on the review page (bean `eb4l`)",
      "prov:value": "| key | button | goes to |\n|---|---|---|\n| `j` | Next | the next item |\n| `k` | Previous | the previous item |\n| `n` | Next with comments | the next block with open comments |\n| `p` | Previous with comments | the previous block with open comments |\n| `u` | Next unreviewed | the next changed block with no reviewer verdict on its CURRENT version (bean `px0t`) |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean px0t"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-16",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The review page, and choosing how to see a change",
      "prov:value": "Each\nchanged block has a **\"Show this change as\"** selector (bean `d903`), and one\nat the top applies to every block:",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean d903"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-17",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "The review page, and choosing how to see a change",
      "prov:value": "| renderer | shows | the default for | needs |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **Word diff of the source** | the Markdown with removed words struck and added words marked: exactly what the author typed | any kind not listed below | the block's prose |\n| **Inline, as rendered** | the block as a reader sees it now, with the change marked in place | `prose`, `remark`, `definition`, `example` | the block's prose |\n| **Pictures, before and after** | a picture of the block on each side, the changed pixels marked, and the share changed in words ([`visual-diff`](visual-diff.md), bean `0rxe`) | `table`, `figure`, `diagram`, `equation`, `simulator` | `visual-diff.json` from the `folio-block-screenshots` Tool |\n| **Side by side** | `main` and the preview next to each other, each scrolled to the block | the same kinds, as the second choice when a build published no pictures | a page on either side |",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean 0rxe"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-18",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Staging retention",
      "prov:value": "Everything else is retained by\ndefault.** Owner, 2026-09-20: *\"change policy, if merged to main, then staging\ngoes away\"* — replacing a blanket retain-on-close.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-19",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "history",
      "cat-harness:section": "Staging retention",
      "prov:value": "**The store DRAINS, and the size threshold depends on it.** Under the old\nretain-on-everything policy the total only ever grew, so any warning point was\nbreached once and stayed breached — a permanent verdict rather than a signal."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-20",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Staging retention",
      "prov:value": "Now what remains is bounded by **concurrent reviews**, not by cumulative\nhistory, which is why the warning point could move from 100 MB to **500 MB**\non 2026-09-20 and start meaning something again: at the measured ~38 MB per\npreview it is about **thirteen concurrent reviews**, and half the documented\n1 GB Pages ceiling.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-21",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Staging retention",
      "prov:value": "That was the state of things until bean `w2g5`: the health\nsweep's `staging-preview-orphans` finding can only ever name a preview whose PR\nis already closed, so the remedy it documented was unreachable for every orphan\nit could report.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean w2g5"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-22",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "**Owner ruling, 2026-10-02 (issue #1868):** *\"for going forward, we should cap\nthe maximum number of previews (<= 10) and rotate old ones off.\"* **Amended\n2026-10-04: \"Cap by size, not count\", budget \"3gb\".** Previews had grown to\n200–780 MB each, so ten of them came to 3–5 GB and any one lasted an hour or\ntwo; a count bounds the total only while preview size holds still, and it did\nnot.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1868",
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-02",
        "2026-10-04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-23",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "The\nbranch passed GitHub's 10 GB Pages artifact limit and the **live** site stopped\ndeploying on 2026-10-01.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-01"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-24",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "**This DOES reach open pull requests, and that is the ruling, not a defect.**\nThe paragraphs above say nothing here touches an open PR; under the cap, the\noldest preview goes whatever its PR's state."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-25",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "The cap — 3 GB of previews in total, the oldest rotated off",
      "prov:value": "The ruling is the confirmation\n[`deletion-requires-confirmation`](../../../skills/conduct/conduct-core/deletion-requires-confirmation.md)\nasks for, given for the class."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-26",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "A closed PR is not an abandoned preview",
      "prov:value": "A session that reuses one branch across successive pull\nrequests has no open PR for the whole gap between one merging and the next\nopening — measured at 5m42s on `claude/brave-hypatia-r820sf`, 2026-09-19, and\nthe sweep landed inside it and called a live branch an orphan.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-19"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-27",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you hand a staging URL to a person (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "**A staging URL is not a deliverable until you have checked the ref, and it is\nnever \"live\" on your say-so.** The rule exists because it was broken here: in\none session an agent relayed the same preview URL to the owner **five times**\nwithout once checking anything, each time off the back of the bot's comment —\nwhich says a workflow *pushed*, not that a site *serves*."
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-28",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Before you hand a staging URL to a person (STRICT)",
      "prov:value": "And where Pages is configured as *Deploy from a branch* — as it is here —\nits builds produce **no workflow runs at all**: measured 2026-09-20,\n`event: page_build` returns `total_count: 0` and there is no\n`pages-build-deployment` workflow to query.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-09-20"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-29",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "date",
      "cat-harness:section": "Say how long, and come back",
      "prov:value": "- **The `stage` job takes about 22 minutes, plus its wait at the rate limit.**\n  Measured 2026-10-31 (run 41191827071): 8 min derived artefacts, 6 min\n  knowledge-graph export, the rest mounting, Jekyll and checks.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-30",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "owner-decision",
      "cat-harness:section": "Say how long, and come back",
      "prov:value": "(It was ~2\n  minutes in 2026-09, before the site grew.) Drafts are staged too, from the\n  first push (owner, 2026-10-31).",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ],
      "dcterms:date": [
        "2026-10-31"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-31",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "issue",
      "cat-harness:section": "Say how long, and come back",
      "prov:value": "Since\n  #1956 the job then waits until `gh-pages` has gone 5 minutes without a\n  staging push and 10 without a main-site one\n  ([`feature-staging`](feature-staging.md) §7), and its PR comment says\n  **queued** with an earliest push time and a live-by time while it waits.",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "#1956"
      ]
    },
    {
      "@id": "skills/ui/ui-core/staging-review.md#provenance-32",
      "@type": "prov:Entity",
      "cat-harness:provenanceKind": "bean",
      "cat-harness:section": "Check for newer cleanup commits on gh-pages",
      "prov:value": "### Check for newer cleanup commits on gh-pages (bean oz5w)",
      "cat-harness:refs": [
        "bean oz5w"
      ]
    }
  ]
}
